<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="5">
  <Content>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" Alignment="Center"><Text Style="Bold+Underline">EPISODE 1: HE'S NOT MY BOYFRIEND</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. AAROGYA HOSPITAL, WARD 3 - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>MEERA (28) opens her eyes. Her left wrist is in a fresh blue cast. She turns her head.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>KARTHIK (30) is asleep in the plastic chair beside her bed, a wet helmet on his lap, studio headphones still round his neck.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>JYOTHI (40s), the night nurse, checks the drip.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JYOTHI</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>లేచారా? మీ boyfriend రెండు గంటల నుంచి ఇక్కడే ఉన్నారు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(hoarse)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Nurse... అతను నా boyfriend కాదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JYOTHI</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Okay.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(beat)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>అయితే వెళ్ళిపొమ్మని చెప్పనా?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera looks at Karthik.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She says nothing.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A long silence.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Jyothi adjusts the drip and leaves.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Karthik stirs, sees her awake, and is instantly up.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>హే. Water కావాలా?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నువ్వు ఇక్కడ ఏం చేస్తున్నావ్?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(pouring water)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ముందు తాగు. తర్వాత మాట్లాడుదాం.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He holds the cup; she drinks. He cranks the bed up a notch without asking.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK (CONT'D)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Flyover మీద scooty జారిందంట. వర్షంలో visor ఎత్తి నడిపావా?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>...లేదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>అబద్ధం.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The corner of her mouth twitches.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. WARD 3 - LATER</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Karthik tapes her cracked phone screen with surgical tape, careful as a sound edit.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>2:40 AM. Karthik dozes upright in the chair, headphones round his neck, one hand resting on the bed rail near her good hand. Not touching.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera watches him. Her lips part.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(whisper)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Karthik...</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He doesn't wake. She doesn't try again.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. WARD 3 - DAWN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Grey light. Karthik's phone buzzes on the bedside table. The screen reads &quot;Amma calling&quot;.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He glances at Meera. Her eyes are closed. He steps to the window.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(into phone)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>హా అమ్మా... లేదు లేదు, నాకేం కాలేదు. Hospital లో ఉన్నా... ఒకళ్ళకి accident అయింది.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SARALA (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఎవరికి రా?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A beat. He looks back at the bed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(into phone)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Office లో ఒకళ్ళు, అమ్మా. Someone from work.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He hangs up. Turns.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera's eyes are open. She heard every word.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She looks at the ceiling. Not at him.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" Alignment="Center" StartsNewPage="Yes"><Text Style="Bold+Underline">EPISODE 2: WHO CALLED YOU?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. AAROGYA HOSPITAL, WARD 3 - MORNING</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A cracked phone screen, held together with surgical tape: &quot;11 missed calls - Karthik ❤&quot;. 9:40 PM to 10:05 PM.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>MEERA, one-handed, opens the contact. Edit. She deletes the heart. Save. It now reads &quot;Karthik&quot;.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The door swings. KARTHIK enters with two paper cups of filter coffee.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Canteen లో filter coffee ఉంది. Doctor పది గంటలకి discharge అన్నారు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(too bright)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Thanks for coming, Karthik. Really. Work లో వాళ్ళ కోసం ఇంత చేస్తారా ఎవరైనా?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He misses it. He hands her the cup and holds it until she has a grip.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>చెయ్యి ఎలా ఉంది?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>అసలు నీకెలా తెలిసింది? నేను ఇక్కడున్నానని.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Hospital వాళ్ళే call చేశారు. నేను నీ emergency contact అంట.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She stares at him.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నేను ఎవరి పేరూ ఇవ్వలేదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(shrugs)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>అయితే ఎవరో ఇచ్చారు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Her phone rings: &quot;Amma&quot;. Meera straightens, swallows, and answers in her office voice.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(into phone)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>హా అమ్మా... Office లో ఉన్నా, meeting లో... అవును, తిన్నాను.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>PADMA (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఇవాళ temple లో Arjun వాళ్ళ అమ్మ కలిశారు తెలుసా? నిన్ను బాగా అడిగారు...</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera's face changes. Karthik notices and watches her.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(into phone)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Okay అమ్మా, తర్వాత call చేస్తా. Bye.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She cuts the call. Karthik raises an eyebrow. She sips her coffee and avoids his eyes.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. AAROGYA RECEPTION - DAY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Discharge papers. Karthik signs as the attendant. JYOTHI, off shift with her coat on, hands Meera a file.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JYOTHI</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఒక్క నిమిషం madam. Emergency contact confirm చేస్తారా, change చేస్తారా?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నేను అసలు ఎవరినీ ఇవ్వలేదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JYOTHI</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(flipping pages)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>మీ పాత file... ఏడు నెలల క్రితం, dengue admission. అప్పుడు రాశారు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She turns the form around. EMERGENCY CONTACT: Karthik, with his number. RELATIONSHIP: Friend.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The handwriting is neat and slanted. It isn't hers.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JYOTHI (CONT'D)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>మార్చాలా?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>...Later.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Then she sees the signature at the bottom of the form: &quot;Arjun Varma&quot;.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The name her mother just said.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Her good hand tightens on the page, crumpling the corner.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" Alignment="Center" StartsNewPage="Yes"><Text Style="Bold+Underline">EPISODE 3: THE FORM</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. AAROGYA RECEPTION - NIGHT (SEVEN MONTHS AGO)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>SUPER: &quot;7 MONTHS AGO&quot;</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Fluorescent glare. ARJUN VARMA (31), crisp shirt, two phones, fills in a form at the counter.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Behind him, MEERA, feverish, is slumped in a wheelchair, whispering into her phone.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(barely audible)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Karthik... నాకు భయంగా ఉంది...</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Arjun's pen stops at &quot;EMERGENCY CONTACT&quot;.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. AAROGYA WARD - DAWN (SEVEN MONTHS AGO)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Through the ward's glass panel, Arjun watches. KARTHIK arrives with an idli parcel and a phone charger. Meera, grey with fever, lights up.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Arjun looks down at the form. He writes a number. Slowly.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. KARTHIK'S CAR - DAY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>SUPER: &quot;NOW&quot;</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Rain. Wipers. Meera in the passenger seat, the folded form in her lap. Karthik hums along to a track on the stereo.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఇది ఎవరిది?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నేనే mix చేశా. Ad jingle. Client కి నచ్చలేదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నాకు నచ్చింది.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He glances at her and smiles. She almost unfolds the form. She doesn't.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. MEERA'S BUILDING, STAIRWELL - DAY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A paper sign on the lift reads &quot;OUT OF ORDER&quot;. Karthik carries her bag up the stairs. She reaches for it.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఇవ్వు, నేను తీసుకెళ్తా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఒక్క చేత్తోనా? నాలుగో floor కి?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నేను ఒక్కదాన్నే manage చేసుకుంటా. ఎప్పుడూ చేసుకున్నా కదా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>తెలుసు. అందుకే ఇవ్వను.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. MEERA'S DOORWAY - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Fourth floor. Both are breathless, standing close. Rain sounds through the stairwell grille.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Karthik.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(beat)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నేను నీకు ఏమవుతాను?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He holds her gaze. Too long. Then he looks down at the bag as he sets it down.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Rest తీసుకో. Tablets టైంకి వేసుకుంటే చాలు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He goes down the stairs. She listens to his footsteps fade.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. MEERA'S FLAT - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She shuts the door and leans on it.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Her phone lights up: &quot;Arjun&quot;.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>ON SCREEN: &quot;Accident gurinchi vinnanu. Are you okay? Can we meet?&quot;</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" Alignment="Center" StartsNewPage="Yes"><Text Style="Bold+Underline">EPISODE 4: THE EX WHO PROPOSED</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. KONDAPUR CAFÉ - DAY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera walks in, blue cast first. ARJUN is already there, standing. Before she can sit:</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఆ form నేనే రాశా, Meeru.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She sits, slowly.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఎందుకు?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She notices there are no phones on the table. He sees her notice.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Bag లో ఉన్నాయి. Silent లో.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(beat)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఆ రాత్రి నీకు 103 జ్వరం. నేను నీ పక్కనే ఉన్నా. నువ్వు phone చేసింది మాత్రం వాడికి.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నాకు గుర్తు లేదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నాకు ఉంది. పొద్దున్న ఆరింటికి వాడు వచ్చాడు. Idli తో, charger తో. నువ్వు నవ్వావ్. ఆ రెండు రోజుల్లో నా వైపు చూసి ఒక్కసారి కూడా అలా నవ్వలేదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera looks down at her coffee.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఏడు నెలలు నిన్నే blame చేశా. నువ్వు వెళ్ళిపోయావని.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నేను వెళ్ళిపోలేదు, Meeru. నువ్వు ఎప్పుడో వెళ్ళిపోయావ్. నేను ఒప్పుకున్నా, అంతే.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Silence. Behind the counter, a milk frother screams.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN (CONT'D)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నేను మారాను. నిజంగా. Calls తగ్గించా. ఒక therapist దగ్గరికి వెళ్తున్నా. వినడం నేర్చుకుంటున్నా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He reaches for her good hand on the table and stops an inch short. He doesn't touch it.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN (CONT'D)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఇంకోసారి try చేద్దామా? ఈసారి నేను ఉంటా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera stares at her cast.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>No yes. No no.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" Alignment="Center" StartsNewPage="Yes"><Text Style="Bold+Underline">EPISODE 5: SOMEONE FROM WORK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. MEERA'S FLAT, FRONT DOOR - EVENING</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera opens the door. KARTHIK stands there with two grocery bags and one mango balanced on top, already rolling up his sleeves.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నీ left hand rest లో ఉంది. నా right hand duty లో ఉంది.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(fighting a smile)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Mango ఎందుకు?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Dessert.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. MEERA'S KITCHEN - EVENING</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Karthik at the stove. Meera sits on the counter, directing one-handed.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఇంకొంచెం అల్లం. ...అంత కాదు!</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He flips a pesarattu. It folds into a mess.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Abstract pesarattu.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She laughs, for the first time since the hospital.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Her phone on the counter lights up. Karthik's eyes go to it.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>ON SCREEN: &quot;Arjun: Dinner Saturday? No pressure.&quot;</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Karthik turns back to the pan.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK (CONT'D)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(even)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నీ ఇష్టం.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera's laugh dies.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>His right hand grips the pan handle, knuckles white. The pesarattu begins to smoke.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>మీ అమ్మకి నేను 'someone from work' నా?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Silence. The pesarattu burns. Smoke curls up.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA (CONT'D)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఆ రోజు నేను నిద్రపోలేదు, Karthik. అంతా విన్నా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He turns off the stove. He doesn't turn around.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Late అయింది. Tablets మర్చిపోకు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He picks up his helmet and goes. The door clicks shut.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. MEERA'S FLAT - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera alone. The burnt pesarattu is still in the pan, the mango untouched.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She opens Arjun's chat and types one-handed: &quot;Saturday. Okay.&quot;</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Her thumb hovers. She sends it.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" Alignment="Center" StartsNewPage="Yes"><Text Style="Bold+Underline">EPISODE 6: PRESENT TENSE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. ROOFTOP RESTAURANT, JUBILEE HILLS - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Fairy lights, the city below. ARJUN slides both his phones face-down onto the table.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఈరోజు only you.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera, surprised, smiles.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Wow. Therapist గారికి thanks చెప్పాలి.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>చెప్తా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(leaning in)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Meeru, నేను అంతా plan చేశా. మార్గశిరలో మంచి ముహూర్తం ఉంది. Kondapur లో 3BHK చూశా, నీ office కి పది నిమిషాలు. అమ్మ already మీ అమ్మతో మాట్లాడింది...</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Arjun, ఒక్క నిమిషం—</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>—నువ్వేం tension పడక్కర్లేదు, అన్నీ నేను చూసుకుంటా. Interiors కూడా నీ taste ప్రకారమే...</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Under the table, Meera's wrist throbs. She winces and presses the cast to her stomach.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He doesn't notice. He's describing a balcony.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She glances at the phone in her lap. No messages. Karthik's name stays silent.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN (CONT'D)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>...ఏమంటావ్?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(caught)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>హా? ...Sorry.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>పర్లేదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He carries on. She checks the phone again. The fourth time.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>It rings: &quot;Karthik&quot;. She answers before the first ring ends.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(into phone)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>హలో?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(voice breaking)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Meera... అమ్మని Warangal లో admit చేశారు. Chest pain. నాకు... నాకేం చేయాలో అర్థం కావట్లేదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She's already standing.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(into phone)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నువ్వు ఎక్కడున్నావ్? ...MGBS దగ్గరే ఉండు. వస్తున్నా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She turns to Arjun. Before she can explain, he's on his feet, keys in hand.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>పద. నేను drop చేస్తా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. ARJUN'S CAR - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Arjun drives fast and clean through wet Hyderabad. He doesn't speak. Meera grips the door handle with her good hand.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Thanks, Arjun.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(eyes on the road)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఏడు నెలల క్రితం కూడా ఇలాగే ఉన్నావ్, Meeru. వాడి కోసం.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. MGBS BUS STAND - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Tube lights. Buses breathing diesel. KARTHIK stands alone under a pillar, lost, a backpack hanging off one shoulder.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera runs to him and takes his hand.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>In the car, Arjun watches through the windshield. He understands. Again.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" Alignment="Center" StartsNewPage="Yes"><Text Style="Bold+Underline">EPISODE 7: WARANGAL</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. OVERNIGHT BUS - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Rain streaks the window. Karthik sits in the aisle seat, staring at nothing. His hand trembles on his knee.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera lays her cast over it, gently, and holds it there.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Neither speaks. The bus rocks on.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. WARANGAL CITY HOSPITAL, CORRIDOR - DAWN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera at the counter, a pharmacy bill clamped in her teeth, signing with her good hand. She talks to a DOCTOR, nods, and types notes into her phone.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Karthik sits frozen on a steel bench, holding his mother's slippers.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera sits beside him.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Mild attack అంట. Stable గా ఉన్నారు. Angiogram రేపు. Medicines తెచ్చా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(barely)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నువ్వు ఎలా... ఇవన్నీ...</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నువ్వేగా నేర్పించావ్.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. SARALA'S ROOM - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Karthik is asleep in the chair beside the bed, head tipped back, headphones round his neck.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>SARALA (56), reading glasses on a chain, studies Meera, who sits on the edge of the visitor's cot.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SARALA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నువ్వే కదా... వాడు రాత్రి ఒంటిగంటకి మాట్లాడేది?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(caught)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>లేదు ఆంటీ, నేను... work లో—</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SARALA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>రాత్రంతా bus లో, ఆ చేత్తో, ఎవరో తెలీని ఆంటీ కోసం వచ్చే అమ్మాయి... work లో ఒకళ్ళు కాదమ్మా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera has no answer.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Sarala looks at her sleeping son.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SARALA (CONT'D)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>వాళ్ళ నాన్న... ఇరవై ఏళ్ళ తర్వాత వెళ్ళిపోయారు. ఒక bag పట్టుకుని. అప్పుడు వీడికి పద్నాలుగేళ్ళు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(beat)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నేను నెలల తరబడి gate దగ్గర నిలబడేదాన్ని. వీడు చూసేవాడు. ఏమీ అనేవాడు కాదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(quiet)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నాకు తెలీదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SARALA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>వాడు ఎవరికీ చెప్పడు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(beat)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>పేరు పెడితే పోగొట్టుకుంటాం అనుకుంటాడు వాడు. పేరు పెట్టకపోతే ఇంకా ఎక్కువ పోగొట్టుకుంటాం అని తెలీదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera looks at Karthik as if seeing him for the first time.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. SARALA'S ROOM - MORNING</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Karthik is awake now. A WARD NURSE holds out a clipboard.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WARD NURSE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Second emergency contact కావాలి sir. Form complete చేయాలి.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Karthik takes the pen and writes his own name on line one.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SARALA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఈ అమ్మాయి number రాయి, Karthik.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Karthik's pen moves to &quot;EMERGENCY CONTACT 2&quot;.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>It stops.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera watches. Sarala watches. The nurse waits.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The pen hovers. Karthik doesn't move.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" Alignment="Center" StartsNewPage="Yes"><Text Style="Bold+Underline">EPISODE 8: THE PEN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. SARALA'S ROOM - MORNING</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The uncapped pen is set down on the blank line.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>అవసరం లేదు, అమ్మా. నేను ఉన్నా కదా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Sarala looks at her son for a long moment. Then she turns to Meera.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SARALA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నీ number నాకు ఇవ్వు. వాడు రాయకపోయినా, నేను రాసుకుంటా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera hesitates, then says the digits quietly. Sarala saves them on her old keypad phone, slowly, while Karthik watches.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>WARD NURSE</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(taking the clipboard)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Okay sir.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. WARANGAL BUS STAND - DAWN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The next day. Steam rises from a tea stall. Karthik and Meera sit on a cement bench with two paper cups. A bus marked &quot;HYDERABAD&quot; idles, engine grumbling.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Angiogram అయిపోయింది. Stent అవసరం లేదంట. Medicines చాలు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(beat)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నువ్వు లేకపోతే నేను—</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(gently)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Karthik.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He stops.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA (CONT'D)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నువ్వు భయపడినప్పుడు నన్ను పిలుస్తావ్. నేను వస్తా. ఎప్పుడూ వస్తా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(beat)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>కానీ ఎవరైనా అడిగితే... 'someone from work'.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Meera, అది—</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నేను నీ emergency ని, Karthik. నీ life ని కాదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He opens his mouth. Nothing comes out.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The bus honks.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>CONDUCTOR (O.S.)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Hyderabad! Hyderabad! బయలుదేరుతోంది!</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera stands. She leaves her tea untouched on the bench.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>అమ్మ దగ్గర ఉండు. ఆమెకి ఇప్పుడు నువ్వు కావాలి.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She boards. She doesn't look back until she's in her seat.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. BUS - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Through the window, Karthik sits on the bench with two paper cups beside him, getting smaller as the bus pulls out.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Her phone rings: &quot;Amma&quot;.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>PADMA (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Meeru! Sunday lunch కి Lakshmi గారు పిలిచారు! Arjun వాళ్ళ ఇంటికి. సరిగ్గా మాట్లాడుకుందాం అన్నారు. వస్తున్నావ్ కదా?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera watches the last of Karthik vanish behind a lorry.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(into phone)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>వస్తాను, అమ్మా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" Alignment="Center" StartsNewPage="Yes"><Text Style="Bold+Underline">EPISODE 9: NEITHER</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. VARMA HOUSE, DINING ROOM, JUBILEE HILLS - DAY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A long table, steel tumblers. LAKSHMI VARMA (50s) sweeps in with a box of sweets and a folded paper before the rice is even served.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>LAKSHMI</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>మార్గశిరలో మంచి ముహూర్తం ఉంది, Padma గారు! పంతులు గారు మూడు dates ఇచ్చారు!</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>PADMA RAO (55) beams. Then her eyes fall on Meera's arm.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>PADMA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Meeru... ఇదేంటి?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>చిన్న accident అమ్మా. Scooty జారింది. ఏం కాలేదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>PADMA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(quiet)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఎప్పుడు?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>...రెండు వారాలైంది.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Padma says nothing more. She sets her tumbler down very carefully. The hurt is total.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>ARJUN, at the head of the table, glances between them. Then his phone buzzes.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Sorry, ఒక్క రెండు నిమిషాలు. Client.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He takes the call right there at the table, in English: &quot;Yes, we can push the deck to Monday...&quot;</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Lakshmi keeps reading out dates. Meera watches Arjun: the same absence, in a nicer shirt.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. VARMA HOUSE, GARDEN - DAY</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Bougainvillea. Arjun comes out, pocketing his phone, contrite.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Sorry. Last time, promise.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Arjun. Form లో నువ్వు correct గానే చూశావ్.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He goes still.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA (CONT'D)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>కానీ conclusion తప్పు. నేను వాడిని పిలిచేది వాడు perfect అని కాదు. నేను ఎవరినీ ఎక్కువ అడగలేదు కాబట్టి. నిన్ను కూడా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(beat)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>లేదు, Arjun.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A long moment. He nods, with dignity.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>ARJUN</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(soft)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>తెలుసు. ఆ రోజు café లోనే తెలుసు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He goes inside.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>PADMA is behind a pillar. She has heard everything. She walks over to Meera.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>PADMA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Accident గురించి నాకు చెప్పలేదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(beat)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నీ మనసు గురించి నీకే చెప్పుకోలేదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera's eyes fill. Padma takes her good hand.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>PADMA (CONT'D)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నీ ఇష్టం, Meeru. నిజంగా నీ ఇష్టం.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. MEERA'S FLAT - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera on the sofa with the hospital app open: &quot;Update emergency contact?&quot;</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She types &quot;Amma&quot;. Her thumb hovers over SAVE.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A notification slides down over it.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>ON SCREEN: &quot;Karthik shared a folder with you: work&quot;</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She taps it. A list loads: voice notes, all in her own voice. &quot;Meera 03-Jan 1.12am&quot;. &quot;Meera 14-Feb 12.58am&quot;. The count at the bottom reads 214.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She presses one. Her own sleepy voice fills the room.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(recorded, laughing)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>...నిద్ర రావట్లేదు. ఏదైనా మాట్లాడు, Karthik.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera puts her hand over her mouth.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" Alignment="Center" StartsNewPage="Yes"><Text Style="Bold+Underline">EPISODE 10: EMERGENCY CONTACT</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. AAROGYA RECEPTION - MORNING</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The blue cast lies on the counter, cut open. Meera rubs her pale, thin wrist.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>JYOTHI slides a form across.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JYOTHI</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Emergency contact update చేయాలా, madam?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera picks up the pen.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A long silence.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The entrance doors hiss open. KARTHIK, unshaven, with a backpack, straight off the Warangal bus, stops a few feet away, breathing hard.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>అమ్మ చెప్పింది... ఇవాళ నీ cast తీసేస్తారని.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A flicker on Meera's face. She and Sarala have been texting.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK (CONT'D)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Meera.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Before she can answer, his phone rings: &quot;Amma calling&quot;.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He looks at it. Looks at her. Then he presses speaker.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK (CONT'D)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(into phone, loud enough for the whole queue)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>అమ్మా. Meera తో ఉన్నా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(beat)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Work లో కాదు. నా మనిషి.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The queue goes quiet. Jyothi stops typing.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SARALA (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(on speaker)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>తెలుసురా. ఇప్పటికి చెప్పావ్.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She hangs up.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Karthik lowers the phone and turns to Meera, unsteady.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>KARTHIK</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>పేరు పెడితే పోతుంది అనుకున్నా. పెట్టకపోతే నువ్వే పోయావ్.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera doesn't run to him. She holds his gaze.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>నేను కూడా ఎప్పుడూ అడగలేదు. ఎవరినీ. అడగడానికి భయం.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(beat)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఇప్పుడు అడుగుతున్నా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>She slides the form and pen to him.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA (CONT'D)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>అయితే నువ్వే రాయి. Relationship column కూడా.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He takes the pen and writes. He doesn't hesitate this time.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Then he reaches into her tote bag, takes out the cut cast, and signs the inside of it.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Her phone buzzes: &quot;Arjun&quot;.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>ON SCREEN: &quot;Pune transfer accepted, next month nunchi. Take care, Meeru. Ee saari, evarini pilavalanukunte vaallani pilu.&quot;</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera reads it twice. A small, sad smile. She types &quot;Thank you, Arjun.&quot; and sends it.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>JYOTHI</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(dry, collecting the form)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>So... boyfriend?</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Meera looks at Karthik. Karthik looks at the floor, then at her.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MEERA</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(smiling)</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>ఇంకా decide చేయలేదు.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Jyothi holds the form. In his handwriting, out of focus, the line reads &quot;Relationship: &quot;.</Text></Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition"><Text>FADE OUT.</Text></Paragraph>
  </Content>
